---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="How to Play — Fantasy World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="Learn how to draft a fantasy World Cup XI from historical squads, pick a formation, and run your team through a simulated knockout tournament with penalty shootouts."
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      Guide
    </p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
        How to play the Fantasy Football World Cup
      </h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-secondary">
      <p>
        Build a fantasy World Cup XI from 100+ old squads. Then watch them play
        the greats in a simulated group stage and knockout tournament. World Cup
        Draft Simulator is a football simulator and a soccer draft game. You pick a
        formation. Choose 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 or 4-2-3-1. You draft your dream team.
      </p>
      <p>
        The match engine simulates the world cup. You get the group stage, the
        knockout bracket, extra time and penalty shootouts. It is a world cup
        simulation and a penalty shootout simulator. It is built around the app.
        You can predict your own tournament online. It is free. It is in the
        browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the US, players find it as a soccer draft game, an online soccer game
        or a free soccer simulation game. Elsewhere, it is the fantasy soccer
        draft and interactive soccer simulator they like. No download. No
        sign-up. It is the easiest browser soccer game to learn fast. The guide
        below shows every step. The FAQ tells how the soccer simulator decides
        matches and how penalty shootouts work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="mt-12 space-y-10">
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">1. Pick your formation</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          Choose between 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 and 4-2-3-1. Your shape locks the
          number of defenders, midfielders and attackers you can draft — every
          pick must fit a position slot.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">2. Draft your XI</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          The draft runs 12 rounds: 11 starters plus 1 bench spot. Each round
          you're offered a random nation + year roster filtered to your
          remaining slots. Use up to 3 rerolls (same nation, different year /
          different nation) before picking. Place each player onto a pitch
          slot — best-position slots are starred. Players carry tier badges
          (elite / star / standard) and chemistry updates as your squad forms.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">3. Review your squad</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          Inspect the XI on the pitch, swap players between slots or the bench,
          then start. Roles come from your formation slots — playing out of
          position is penalized, and same-nation players get a chemistry boost.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">4. Run the tournament</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          Your squad joins 3 opponents (2 weak draws, 1 strong historical team)
          in a round-robin group. Your 3 group matches play out segment by
          segment and auto-start on entry; the rest are pre-simulated. Top 2
          advance to a knockout bracket (round of 16 → quarter-final →
          semi-final → final) against fresh opponents. Ties go to extra time,
          then penalty shootouts.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">5. Results &amp; replay</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          View the final standing, squad stats, and replay any match. Lose and
          you can play again with the same team; champions get one shot only.
          Start a fresh draft any time.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <p>
          The full loop of World Cup Draft Simulator is short. That is the appeal
          of a free browser soccer game. You start by choosing a football
          formation. The soccer simulator respects positions. Your choice locks
          how many defenders, midfielders and attackers you can draft. You pick
          over 12 rounds. A 4-3-3 leans attack. A 3-5-2 owns the middle. A 4-4-2
          balances. A 4-2-3-1 controls the game.
        </p>
        <p>
          Next, the football draft simulator shows you old World Cup squads. You
          place each player in the best slot. You watch chemistry update. You get
          a few rerolls if the board is bad. Same-nation picks get a chemistry
          boost. So a smart world cup dream team builder beats a team of stars.
        </p>
        <p>
          When your XI is set, the match engine simulates the group stage. It
          plays live, part by part. The rest of the bracket is pre-simulated. So
          the whole world cup simulation ends fast. Knockout ties go to extra
          time. Then a penalty shootout simulator decides. Five kicks each. Then
          sudden death. This is the drama fans love.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are not predicting real 2026 results. You use the world cup
          simulator 2026 mode to predict your own cup. Players call it a world cup
          predictor for their cup. It is a soccer game with no download. It runs on
          any device. Your save stays on your device. It is a fantasy soccer draft
          where the draft matters most.
        </p>
        <p>
          When the final ends, you can replay any match. Compare squad stats.
          Start a fresh draft. The steps above break this into five moves. The FAQ
          explains the football simulation, the formations and the penalty
          shootouts. Call it an interactive soccer simulator. Or call it the world
          cup fantasy game. Or the easiest online soccer game to open between
          matches. The path is the same. Shape, draft, simulate, repeat.
        </p>
      </div>

    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-white/10 pt-10 text-center">
      <a
        href="/game"
        class="inline-block rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
      >
        Start drafting
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
      <p class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
        FAQ
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl">
        Questions about the simulator
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">What is World Cup Draft Simulator?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            It is a free browser soccer game and a fantasy soccer draft tool. You
            build a dream XI from 100+ old World Cup squads. The app simulates a
            full tournament. You get the group stage, the knockout bracket and
            penalty shootouts. It predicts your final result.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">How does the football simulation work?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Every match is simulated part by part by the match engine. It uses
            player ratings, football formations and same-nation chemistry. The
            world cup simulation plays group games live. The rest of the bracket
            is pre-simulated.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">What formations can I draft?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Four shapes work: 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 and 4-2-3-1. Your formation locks
            the defender, midfielder and attacker slots. You fill them over 12
            draft rounds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">How do penalty shootouts work?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Knockout ties go to extra time. Then a penalty shootout simulator
            decides. Each side takes five kicks. After that, it is sudden death.
            It is like real world cup penalty shootouts, but made by the game.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">Is it free and does it need a download?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Yes. It is a free soccer simulation game and a browser soccer game. No
            download. No sign-up. Play online on any device.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify({
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          mainEntity: [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "What is World Cup Draft Simulator?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "It is a free browser soccer game and a fantasy soccer draft tool. You build a dream XI from 100+ old World Cup squads. The app simulates a full tournament. You get the group stage, the knockout bracket and penalty shootouts. It predicts your final result.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "How does the football simulation work?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Every match is simulated part by part by the match engine. It uses player ratings, football formations and same-nation chemistry. The world cup simulation plays group games live. The rest of the bracket is pre-simulated.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "What formations can I draft?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Four shapes work: 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 and 4-2-3-1. Your formation locks the defender, midfielder and attacker slots. You fill them over 12 draft rounds.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "How do penalty shootouts work?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Knockout ties go to extra time. Then a penalty shootout simulator decides. Each side takes five kicks. After that, it is sudden death. It is like real world cup penalty shootouts, but made by the game.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "Is it free and does it need a download?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Yes. It is a free soccer simulation game and a browser soccer game. No download. No sign-up. Play online on any device.",
              },
            },
          ],
        })}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
